{
  "tema": 7121,
  "slug": "presente-orden",
  "titulo": "The present tense to give orders, advice or make requests",
  "subtitulo": "Vas a la tienda y compras pan.",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "In colloquial Spanish, the present indicative can work like a command, for orders, requests and advice: Vas a la tienda y me compras tortillas. ¿Me pasas la sal? Pues vas y hablas con ella. It sounds informal and sometimes firm.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **present tense** can replace the imperative to tell someone what to do. It sounds **colloquial**: friendly in a request, firm in an order."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "orders",
              "texto": "**Niños, se ponen los suéteres y nos vamos.**"
            },
            {
              "forma": "requests",
              "texto": "**¿Me pasas la sal?** (very common in Mexico)"
            },
            {
              "forma": "advice",
              "texto": "**Pues vas y hablas con ella.**"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Often with **y** linking steps: **vas, buscas, me avisas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: describing the action as if it's already happening makes it hard to say no."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Niños, ==se ponen== los suéteres y ==nos vamos==.",
              "en": "Kids, put on your sweaters and let's go."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ahorita ==vas== a la tienda y me ==compras== tortillas, por favor.",
              "en": "Go to the store right now and buy me tortillas, please."
            },
            {
              "es": "—Carmen está enojada. —Pues ==vas== y ==hablas== con ella.",
              "en": "—Carmen is upset. —Well, go and talk to her."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Me ==pasas== la sal?",
              "en": "Can you pass me the salt?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Tú te ==callas== y me ==escuchas==.",
              "en": "You be quiet and listen to me."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
